Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:40:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 112/191] [ae-patch] Keep a Claude Code subagent running until
 its parent records its return

A transcript lull no longer reads as completion: the subagent.status idle is held for a Claude Code subagent child until the parent records its completion marker, republishing the child's busy status with the lull's response, blocked and background fields. The newly recorded completion publishes the child's terminal status (failed for a failure, idle otherwise); a replayed one only settles a child with no cached status. A held child whose conversation stays quiet for 60 minutes is settled idle by a server-side timer, for children a host restart left without a completion.
